Subject: [PATCH] linux: ignore battery interfaces without charge information

The Qualcomm SMBB charger exposes smbb-bif as type Battery, with status,
presence and health, but no capacity, energy or charge measurements. On an
LG Fx0 the supply produces a NaN percentage and an erroneous UPower power-off.

Skip battery interfaces that have none of the charge-information attributes
consumed by the backends. Check attribute presence, retaining valid zero
capacity/charge values. Reject before trying either battery backend, since
the generic supply fallback does not support system batteries.

Add a regression fixture matching the charger interface. Existing empty-battery,
charge/energy, capacity-level and critical-action tests remain required.
This does not implement native fuel gauging or qualify the Fx0 charging policy.

---
--- a/src/linux/up-enumerator-udev.c
+++ b/src/linux/up-enumerator-udev.c
@@ -110,6 +110,21 @@
 	subsys = g_udev_device_get_subsystem (native);
 	if (g_strcmp0 (subsys, "power_supply") == 0) {
 		UpDevice *device;
+		const gchar *type = g_udev_device_get_sysfs_attr (native, "type");
+
+		/* Some charger interfaces are labelled Battery but cannot report
+		 * charge. Do not turn missing measurements into an empty battery.
+		 * Check attribute presence so a valid zero reading is retained.
+		 */
+		if (type && g_ascii_strcasecmp (type, "battery") == 0 &&
+		    !g_udev_device_has_sysfs_attr_uncached (native, "capacity") &&
+		    !g_udev_device_has_sysfs_attr_uncached (native, "capacity_level") &&
+		    !g_udev_device_has_sysfs_attr_uncached (native, "energy_now") &&
+		    !g_udev_device_has_sysfs_attr_uncached (native, "energy_avg") &&
+		    !g_udev_device_has_sysfs_attr_uncached (native, "charge_now")) {
+			g_debug ("Ignoring battery interface without charge information");
+			return NULL;
+		}
 
 		device = g_initable_new (UP_TYPE_DEVICE_SUPPLY_BATTERY, NULL, NULL,
 		                       "daemon", daemon,
--- a/src/linux/integration-test.py
+++ b/src/linux/integration-test.py
@@ -627,6 +627,29 @@
             self.get_dbus_dev_property(bat0_up, "State"), UP_DEVICE_STATE_CHARGING
         )
 
+    def test_battery_without_charge_information(self):
+        """A charger battery interface has no usable state-of-charge data."""
+        self.testbed.add_device(
+            "power_supply",
+            "smbb-bif",
+            None,
+            [
+                "type", "Battery",
+                "present", "1",
+                "status", "Discharging",
+                "health", "Overheat",
+                "voltage_min_design", "3000000",
+            ],
+            [],
+        )
+
+        self.start_daemon()
+        self.assertEqual(self.proxy.EnumerateDevices(), [])
+        self.assertEqual(
+            self.get_dbus_display_property("WarningLevel"), UP_DEVICE_LEVEL_NONE
+        )
+        self.stop_daemon()
+
     def test_battery_ac(self):
         """properties with dynamic battery/AC"""
 
